85d3807a3e4e05be6a3d58b1418e786d","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?u=f0c85fe8c24debe91dc14d7efa97b51a19250b47&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","login":"kitbdev","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev"},"body":"The replacing completion logic is not correct. When there is a symbol after the caret (including space) it should never be replaced.\r\nWhen using the accept mode, it should not remove any text, and when using the replace mode, all text should be replaced, not just one letter.\r\n\r\nThe code completion box should move with the caret, so it is clear that using completion will not actually replace the current value. Currently, it is confusing if you are used to the regular behavior and there is no way to tell the difference.\r\n\r\nMaybe it should also remain open after using the completion. Currently it stays open only if not using the completion until it gets to a length of 4. If a user wants to use the completion they have to repeatedly query it.\r\n\r\nAdding code edit completion test cases would be good.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100521#pullrequestreview-2533097750","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100521","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-01-06T23:33:24Z"}]